# Canonical TPC-H Q12/Q13 row counts for scripts/tpch-spotcheck.sh.
#
# These are the expected row counts for the dataset currently loaded in
# bench/tpch/runtime_goopg/data (HammerDB TPC-H build, SF=1 by default —
# see env_goopg.sh TPCH_SCALE_FACT).
#
# Evidence:
#   - Q12 = 2 is structurally invariant: the query is GROUP BY l_shipmode
#     with l_shipmode IN ('MAIL', 'SHIP'), so any correctly-loaded dataset
#     returns exactly 2 rows. Observed rows=2 in every clean run on record
#     (bench/tpch/logs/m0059..m0070 22-query sweeps, May 2026;
#     tpch_runner_goopg_m0093_20260511_183304.log).
#   - Q13 = 35 on the canonical dataset (bench/tpch/logs/m0059..m0070
#     sweeps; memory note feedback_tpch_pre_commit_gates: "Q12 must return
#     2 rows, Q13 must return 35 rows").
#
# CAUTION — Q13 is load-dependent: it is GROUP BY c_count over a random
# order distribution, so a *fresh* HammerDB data load can legitimately
# shift it by ±1 (the 2026-05-11 reload produced Q13=36, see
# tpch_runner_goopg_m0093_20260511_183304.log). After every fresh
# build_schema_goopg.sh, re-pin Q13_EXPECTED from one trusted run.
#
# Known FAILURE signatures (revert the commit immediately):
#   Q12=0 / Q13=2  (m0071 Stage-B silent regression)
Q12_EXPECTED=2
Q13_EXPECTED=35
